      "date_raw": "Sat, 1 Jun 2024 09:18:32 -0600",
      "body": "On Sat, Jun 01, 2024, Martin Juh�s via AMBER wrote:\n>\n>I am facing an issue within my amber installation. It seems like parmed has\n>not been installed. I first noticed it when pdb4amber was not running, but\n>then I noticed even parmed binary has not been installed. Can you help me\n>with this? I used common run_cmake installation.\nFirst: go to the amber24_src/build folder, and look at the cmake.log file.\nExamine the \"Build report\": is parmed listed as \"being built\" or \"not being\nbuilt\"? If the latter, the log file should give a reason.\nIf parmed is scheduled to be built, re-run the \"make install\" step, probably\nafter running \"./clean_build\" to get a fresh start. Save the output to some\nlog file, and look for references to parmed.\n..good luck...dac",
